  "verdict": "correction_required",
  "humanApproval": false,
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "evidencePath": "packages/workflow-control/src/storage.ts",
      "location": "WorkflowStore.dispatchTransitionMutation; reconciliation.ts: execute and reconcilePrepared",
      "reason": "Dispatch derives its owner and fencing token from a newly loaded transition instead of requiring the caller's fence. A successor can acquire expired leases and adopt the prepared transition after the broker's assertTransitionLeases call but before dispatchTransitionMutation reads it. The guard then verifies the successor's authority and invokes the old broker's closure, which still passes the old transition to port.mutate. This allows a fenced-out caller to initiate an effect using authority borrowed from the successor. The checks inside the writer transaction only compare against the guard's newly loaded transition, so they do not catch this race.",
      "proposedCorrection": "Pass the caller's expected owner, run epoch and resource lease epochs into dispatchTransitionMutation. Compare them with the persisted transition and current leases under the writer reservation before invoking dispatch. Prefer passing the validated persisted transition into the callback. Add execution and recovery regressions that adopt the transition between the preliminary lease check and entry into the dispatch guard, and assert zero old-owner mutation calls."
    }
  ],
  "resolvedPriorFindings": [
    {
      "finding": "Ordinary Git delivery permits lease expiry during blocking adapter observations",
      "assessment": "Resolved at the supplied adapter boundaries. The broker supplies assertDispatch, and the per-call Git adapter invokes it immediately before commit-tree, update-ref, create-ref and remote-client push invocation. The callback requires the matching active writer reservation and checks current leases and durable authority. Bootstrap retains its synchronous reservation reuse and additional checks."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Beads/Dolt effects bypass document verification after awaited observations",
      "assessment": "The document-verification gap is resolved for execution and recovery: both now verify source bytes durably and check approval, cancellation and leases under a writer reservation before invoking the port. The new tests cover changes during suspended observations. Caller fencing remains incomplete because of the separate adoption race described above."
    }
  ],
  "coverageLimits": [
    "Static review of supplied evidence only. No commands executed, state changed or hashes independently recomputed.",
    "New test reruns are pending. The reported earlier suite and container results do not establish passing results for these final repairs.",
    "The Git expiry regression checks that the ref remains unchanged after expiry at write-tree; it does not independently count commit-tree invocations or cover expiry between commit-tree and update-ref, during create-ref observations, or before remote push.",
    "The supplied Beads/Dolt regressions replace leases during observation, before the preliminary lease check. They do not cover adoption between that check and dispatch guard entry.",
    "Production ordinary remote Git, GitHub and Beads client implementations are absent. Actual external dispatch before any internal asynchronous suspension cannot be established from their interfaces.",
    "Cleanup exceptions remain excluded for Beads operations. Broader cleanup and recovery acceptance, complete DB-T01–11 coverage, hosted checks and managed pilot readiness are not established by this bounded follow-up."
  ]
}
